      <workList xml:id="workDesc_dc7d1f98">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e221218">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_6e5bd783">A1:004</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="fr">Concerto à quatre</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_34ce03b4">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_20">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_21_0">
               <p xml:id="idm114">The only source to the present concerto for 'flauto dolce' is a manuscript copy produced in 1906 by <persName xml:id="idm115" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Alphonse Goyens</persName>. It is based on a set of instrumental parts, presumably from the eighteenth century, to which he had access. It is highly likely that the transcription was carried out at the instigation of <persName xml:id="idm116" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Alfred Wotquenne</persName>, the librarian of the Bibliotheque du Conservatoire royale in Brussels and whose signature appears on the title page. It is the only known so-called concerto that Scheibe wrote for the recorder suggesting that it might be an early work as the popularity of the instrument declined rapidly among the younger generation of composers from the beginning of the eighteenth century.</p>
            </history>
